/* Generated by tools/build-docs-bundle.mjs. Edit assets/content/docs/ instead. */
(function () {
  'use strict';
  var bodies = {
  "overview/introduction": "\u003cp>CoreArmorX is a Paper-only vanilla+ armor progression plugin for Minecraft/Paper 1.21.11 or newer and Java 21 or newer. It uses normal crafting and vanilla item behavior instead of custom menus, economies or databases.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"runtime-model\">Two item models\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Normal upgraded armor uses its Bukkit material as the source of truth and receives no CoreArmorX persistent data. Skinned netherite armor stores its clean material, visual skin, original lore state, inventory model mode and optional cosmetic durability in Paper persistent data.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"standalone-scope\">Standalone scope\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreArmorX does not require Vault, PlaceholderAPI, a database, a GUI library, a resource pack, CoreToolsX or a custom-item plugin. A permissions plugin such as LuckPerms is useful only when progression locks are enabled.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"defaults\">Conservative defaults\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Progression locks are disabled.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Skin durability is disabled.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Fire/lava skin stripping is disabled.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Foreign persistent data blocks transformations.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Protected direct recipes are replaced by the progression path.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n",
  "overview/progression-and-recipes": "\u003cp>CoreArmorX routes protected direct armor crafting through configurable upgrade definitions. The bundled path is leather → copper → chainmail → iron → diamond, with iron → gold and iron helmet → turtle helmet as alternate endpoints.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"default-routes\">Default routes\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>LEATHER → COPPER\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>COPPER → CHAINMAIL\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>CHAINMAIL → IRON\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>IRON → DIAMOND\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>IRON → GOLD\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>IRON_HELMET → TURTLE_HELMET\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"recipe-model\">Recipe model\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Ingredient groups accept configured Bukkit materials. Runtime matching requires separate one-item ingredient slots; stacking the cost into one slot is intentionally rejected. Static recipe-book recipes can expose discovery while the runtime matcher validates the real item, cost, metadata and permission.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"protected-vanilla-recipes\">Protected vanilla recipes\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>With \u003ccode>recipes.override-vanilla-equipment-recipes: true\u003c/code>, protected direct outputs use their matching \u003ccode>minecraft:*\u003c/code> keys. Leather armor crafting and vanilla diamond-to-netherite smithing are not changed. Original protected recipes return when the override is disabled or the plugin stops.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"costs\">Costs and durability\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>VANILLA_RECIPE_COST\u003c/code> uses 5/8/7/4 ingredients for helmet/chestplate/leggings/boots. \u003ccode>CUSTOM\u003c/code> reads a positive \u003ccode>count\u003c/code>. Upgrade output durability can be \u003ccode>REFILL\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>KEEP_DAMAGE\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>KEEP_PERCENTAGE\u003c/code>; repair cost preservation is separately configurable.\u003c/p>\n",
  "overview/netherite-skins": "\u003cp>Skin recipes accept clean netherite armor and convert it to a vanilla visual material while applying a netherite-equivalent armor profile. Already-skinned pieces must be stripped before another skin can be applied.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"default-skins\">Default skins\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Leather, copper, chainmail, iron, gold and diamond skins cover helmet, chestplate, leggings and boots. Leather skins remain compatible with vanilla dye behavior.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"inventory-models\">Inventory models\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>REAL_TIER\u003c/code> is the default and keeps a netherite inventory model while the equipped appearance follows the visual skin. \u003ccode>VISUAL_SKIN\u003c/code> shows the visual material icon. CoreArmorX needs no resource pack for either mode.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"lore\">Lore and placeholders\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>skins.lore.generated-lines\u003c/code> controls the final generated lore. A list entry exactly equal to \u003ccode>{item_lore}\u003c/code> reinserts the saved original lore; omitting it hides but does not discard the snapshot. Placeholders cover skin, identifiers, clean/visual/real materials, leather color formats and cosmetic durability values.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"skin-durability\">Cosmetic durability\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Modes are \u003ccode>DISABLED\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>GLOBAL\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>BY_SKIN\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>BY_ITEM\u003c/code>. Damage currently mirrors real item damage with a multiplier. On break, the only supported action is \u003ccode>REMOVE_SKIN\u003c/code>. Mending can be disabled, split repair points or double the repair into cosmetic durability.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"removal-and-fire\">Removal and fire\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>By default, a skinned piece plus shears returns clean netherite armor and damages the shears by one. Dropped skinned armor is protected from configured fire/lava destruction while stripping is disabled. When enabled, those causes strip the skin instead of destroying the item.\u003c/p>\n",
  "overview/item-safety": "\u003cp>CoreArmorX preserves supported data while changing armor materials: custom name, original lore, enchantments, durability damage, max damage where supported, repair cost, trims, flags, unbreakable state, compatible custom data and non-CoreArmorX persistent data.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"foreign-data\">Foreign custom data\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>BLOCK_IF_DETECTED\u003c/code> is the safe default: transformations stop when foreign persistent data is present. \u003ccode>REPLACE_ANYWAY\u003c/code> permits conversion and should be used only when the administrator knows the other item format is compatible.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"identity\">CoreArmorX identity\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Only skinned armor and its internal skin state carry CoreArmorX identity. Normal upgraded armor remains ordinary vanilla armor. This boundary avoids making every progression output dependent on the plugin.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"admin-repair\">Inspection and repair\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>/corearmorx inspect\u003c/code> reports the held item’s current and clean materials, skin, model mode, lore snapshot and durability state. \u003ccode>/corearmorx fixitem\u003c/code> reapplies the configured profile and display to a recognized skinned item; it is not a generic item converter.\u003c/p>\n",
  "getting-started/installation": "\u003ch2 id=\"requirements\">Requirements\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Paper/Minecraft 1.21.11 or newer.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Java 21 or newer.\u003c/li>\u003cli>The CoreArmorX JAR from \u003ca href=\"https://modrinth.com/plugin/corearmorx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Modrinth\u003c/a>.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"download\">Download\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Use the public Modrinth project for stable builds. The private plugin source repository is not a download or documentation endpoint.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"install\">Installation flow\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\u003cli>Stop the Paper server.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Place \u003ccode>CoreArmorX-2026.1.2.jar\u003c/code> in \u003ccode>plugins/\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Start once and confirm the enable message has no configuration warnings.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Edit files under \u003ccode>plugins/CoreArmorX/\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Run \u003ccode>/corearmorx reload\u003c/code> after normal YAML changes.\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\n\u003ch2 id=\"generated-files\">Generated files\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre>\u003ccode>plugins/CoreArmorX/\n├── config.yml\n├── armor-upgrades.yml\n├── armor-skins.yml\n└── messages.yml\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>plugin.yml\u003c/code> is internal JAR metadata, not a server configuration file.\u003c/p>\n",
  "getting-started/reload-vs-restart": "\u003ch2 id=\"safe-to-reload\">Safe with /corearmorx reload\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The command reloads all four YAML files, rebuilds validated definitions, removes and re-registers CoreArmorX recipes, and normalizes the configured skin fire-resistance policy on online players’ items.\u003c/p>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Runtime toggles and recipe-book behavior.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Upgrade and skin definitions.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Messages and permission strings stored in YAML.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Lore templates.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Inventory model and cosmetic durability for newly created or subsequently refreshed skinned items.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"restart-required\">Restart required\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Replacing the plugin JAR.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Changing Paper or Minecraft runtime.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Recovering from startup/classloading errors.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Performing a clean-boot validation after broad configuration edits.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"existing-files\">Existing files are not merged\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A reload does not add newly packaged keys to an existing YAML file. After an upgrade, compare the installed files with the synchronized defaults before relying on a new option.\u003c/p>\n",
  "getting-started/first-validation": "\u003ch2 id=\"clean-setup\">Clean setup\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\u003cli>Confirm version 2026.1.2 enables on Paper 1.21.11+ with Java 21+.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Run \u003ccode>/corearmorx reload\u003c/code> and review every warning.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Craft one item through each enabled upgrade branch using separate one-item ingredient slots.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Apply, inspect, fix and remove one netherite skin.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Test leather dyeing and lore if leather skins are enabled.\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\n\u003ch2 id=\"permissions\">Permission validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>If progression locks are enabled, test with a non-operator account. Verify upgrade, skin, usage and bypass behavior independently.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"safety\">Safety validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Test a foreign custom item before changing \u003ccode>BLOCK_IF_DETECTED\u003c/code>. If fire/lava stripping is changed, test both a dropped skinned item and the restored clean netherite result.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"production-validation-checklist\">Production checklist\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Keep a copy of the active YAML files.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Confirm the intended protected vanilla recipes are replaced.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Check recipe-book discovery separately from runtime crafting.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Do not assume a successful reload refreshes every existing item immediately.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n",
  "paper/files": "\u003cp>CoreArmorX generates four administrator-facing files in \u003ccode>plugins/CoreArmorX/\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"file-layout\">Runtime folder\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The folder contains only the four YAML defaults below. It does not contain a public descriptor or player progression database.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"config-yml\">config.yml\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Global recipe behavior, ingredient groups, upgrade defaults, lore, leather color, inventory model, removal, fire/lava handling, progression locks and custom-item safety.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"armor-upgrades-yml\">armor-upgrades.yml\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Named progression routes with source/target tiers or exact materials, ingredients, costs and permissions.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"armor-skins-yml\">armor-skins.yml\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Named netherite skins, output materials and optional cosmetic durability.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"messages-yml\">messages.yml\u003c/h2>\u003cp>MiniMessage text for commands, crafting, progression and item inspection.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"excluded-files\">Not public configuration\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>plugin.yml\u003c/code> stays inside the JAR and is intentionally excluded from configuration sync, raw downloads and the documentation catalog.\u003c/p>\n",
  "paper/config-yml": "\u003cp>This file controls global behavior. Exact comments and defaults are mounted below from the allow-listed plugin resource.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"key-map\">Key map\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.debug\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>recipes.override-vanilla-equipment-recipes\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>recipes.blocked-message-cooldown-ticks\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>recipes.recipe-book.enabled\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>ingredient-groups.COPPER_ARMOR_MATERIALS\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CHAINMAIL_ARMOR_MATERIALS\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>IRON_ARMOR_MATERIALS\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>GOLD_ARMOR_MATERIALS\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>DIAMOND_ARMOR_MATERIALS\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>TURTLE_HELMET_MATERIALS\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>upgrades.enabled\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>cost-mode\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>durability-mode\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>preserve-repair-cost\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>skins.enabled\u003c/code>; \u003ccode>skins.lore.enabled\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>format\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>generated-lines\u003c/code>; \u003ccode>skins.leather-color.placeholders\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>square-character\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>default-color.mode\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>default-color.custom-hex\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>armor-skins.inventory-model.mode\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>skin-removal.enabled\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>tool\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>consume-tool\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>damage-tool\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>damage-amount\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>skin-stripping.enabled\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>causes\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>mode\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>progression-locks.enabled\u003c/code>; \u003ccode>blocks.crafting\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>blocks.upgrades\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>blocks.usage\u003c/code>; \u003ccode>permissions.bypass\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>permissions.usage-prefix\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>compatibility.custom-items.behavior\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"supported-values\">Supported values\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Costs: \u003ccode>VANILLA_RECIPE_COST|CUSTOM\u003c/code>. Upgrade durability: \u003ccode>REFILL|KEEP_DAMAGE|KEEP_PERCENTAGE\u003c/code>. Inventory: \u003ccode>REAL_TIER|VISUAL_SKIN\u003c/code>. Leather fallback: \u003ccode>LEATHER_DEFAULT|CUSTOM_HEX\u003c/code>. Stripping mode is currently only \u003ccode>STRIP_SKIN\u003c/code>. Custom-item behavior: \u003ccode>BLOCK_IF_DETECTED|REPLACE_ANYWAY\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/config.yml\">\u003c/div>\n",
  "paper/armor-upgrades-yml": "\u003cp>Each child of \u003ccode>upgrades\u003c/code> is an independent route.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"definition-schema\">Definition schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>enabled\u003c/code>: include the route.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>from-tier\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>from-material\u003c/code>: source.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>to-tier\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>to-material\u003c/code>: output.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>ingredient\u003c/code>: Bukkit material or a group from \u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>cost-mode\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>VANILLA_RECIPE_COST\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>CUSTOM\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>count\u003c/code>: positive custom cost.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>permission\u003c/code>: checked when progression locks apply.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"defaults\">Bundled definitions\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>leather_to_copper\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>copper_to_chainmail\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>chainmail_to_iron\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>iron_to_gold\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>iron_to_diamond\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>iron_helmet_to_turtle\u003c/code>. Supported tiers are leather, copper, chainmail, iron, gold, diamond and netherite; exact material fields support special one-piece routes.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"validation\">Validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Missing endpoints, unknown material/group values and invalid costs disable the affected definition with a warning instead of creating an unsafe recipe.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/armor-upgrades.yml\">\u003c/div>\n",
  "paper/armor-skins-yml": "\u003cp>This file defines netherite visual skins and the optional cosmetic durability layer.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"skin-schema\">Skin definition schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>skins.&lt;id&gt;\u003c/code> supports \u003ccode>enabled\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>display-name\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ingredient\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>cost-mode\u003c/code>, positive custom \u003ccode>count\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>dyeable\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>permission\u003c/code>, and \u003ccode>output-materials.{helmet,chestplate,leggings,boots}\u003c/code>. Defaults are leather, copper, chainmail, iron, gold and diamond.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"durability-schema\">Cosmetic durability schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>skin-durability.mode\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>DISABLED|GLOBAL|BY_SKIN|BY_ITEM\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>global.max-durability\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>by-skin.default-max-durability\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>by-skin.materials.&lt;skin&gt;\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>by-item.default-max-durability\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>by-item.materials.&lt;skin&gt;.{default-max-durability,helmet,chestplate,leggings,boots}\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>damage.mode\u003c/code> (currently only \u003ccode>MIRROR_REAL_DAMAGE\u003c/code>) and \u003ccode>damage.multiplier\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>on-break\u003c/code> (currently only \u003ccode>REMOVE_SKIN\u003c/code>).\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>mending.mode\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>DISABLED|SPLIT|DOUBLE\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>placeholders.{disabled-value,bar-segments,bar-full,bar-empty}\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/armor-skins.yml\">\u003c/div>\n",
  "paper/messages-yml": "\u003cp>Messages use Adventure MiniMessage. The configured prefix is prepended by the message service. A placeholder is available only where that message’s event supplies it.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"key-map\">Message key map\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>prefix\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>commands.{no-permission,unknown,reloaded,version,help-header,help-version,help-reload,help-inspect,help-fixitem,player-only}\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>crafting.{blocked-vanilla-craft,no-permission,custom-item-blocked}\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>progression.usage-blocked\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>admin.{inspect-empty-hand,fix-empty-hand,fix-not-skinned,fixed}\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>admin.inspect.{header,current-material,clean-material,visual-skin,inventory-model-mode,has-core-data,generated-lore,original-lore,skin-durability,skin-durability-disabled,leather-color,tier,piece}\u003c/code>\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"placeholders\">Placeholders\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Command/version and inspection messages use the placeholders shown in the synchronized comments, such as \u003ccode>{version}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{material}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{skin}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{mode}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{damage}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{remaining}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{max}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{percent}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{color}\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>{tier}\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>{piece}\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/messages.yml\">\u003c/div>\n",
  "reference/command-reference": "\u003ctable>\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Command\u003c/th>\u003cth>Behavior\u003c/th>\u003cth>Permission\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/corearmorx help\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Shows commands available to the sender.\u003c/td>\u003ctd>None\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/corearmorx version\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Shows the installed version.\u003c/td>\u003ctd>None\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/corearmorx reload\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Reloads configuration, definitions, messages and recipes.\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corearmorx.admin.reload\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/corearmorx inspect\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Inspects the held armor item; player-only.\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corearmorx.admin.inspect\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/corearmorx fixitem\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Refreshes a recognized held skinned item; player-only.\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corearmorx.admin.fixitem\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>Alias: \u003ccode>/cax\u003c/code>. Unknown subcommands show the configured help hint. Tab completion exposes admin subcommands only when the sender has the matching permission.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/permission-reference": "\u003ch2 id=\"admin\">Administration\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>corearmorx.admin\u003c/code> — operator-default aggregate for reload, inspect, fixitem and progression bypass.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>corearmorx.admin.reload\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.inspect\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.fixitem\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>corearmorx.progression.bypass\u003c/code> — bypasses progression checks.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"skins\">Skins\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>corearmorx.skin.*\u003c/code> aggregates \u003ccode>.leather\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.copper\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.chainmail\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.iron\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.gold\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>.diamond\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"upgrades\">Upgrades\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>corearmorx.upgrade.*\u003c/code> aggregates \u003ccode>.leather_to_copper\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.copper_to_chainmail\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.chainmail_to_iron\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.iron_to_gold\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>.iron_to_diamond\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>.iron_helmet_to_turtle\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"usage\">Usage locks\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>corearmorx.use.*\u003c/code> aggregates leather, copper, chainmail, iron, gold, diamond, netherite and turtle tier nodes. Usage checks run only when progression locks and \u003ccode>blocks.usage\u003c/code> are enabled. Configured definition permission strings and usage prefix can be changed in YAML.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/troubleshooting-quick-reference": "\u003ch2 id=\"startup\">Plugin does not enable\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Confirm Paper/Minecraft 1.21.11+, Java 21+, the correct JAR and complete startup logs. Restart after correcting classloading/runtime problems.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"recipe-output\">A recipe appears but will not craft\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Use separate one-item ingredient slots. Check the route/skin is enabled, ingredient group is valid, permission locks, whether the base is already skinned and custom-item compatibility.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"vanilla-recipe\">A direct vanilla recipe still works\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Check \u003ccode>recipes.override-vanilla-equipment-recipes\u003c/code>, reload, and review warnings. Leather crafting and diamond-to-netherite smithing are intentionally untouched.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"reload\">Reload does not change an existing item\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Reload changes definitions for new/refreshed items. Use \u003ccode>/corearmorx fixitem\u003c/code> on a recognized skinned item when its display/profile needs refresh; restart only for the documented restart boundaries.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"custom-item\">A custom item is blocked\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The safe default rejects foreign PDC. Do not choose \u003ccode>REPLACE_ANYWAY\u003c/code> until compatibility is understood.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"skin-fire\">A dropped skin survives fire or lava\u003c/h2>\u003cp>This is the default protection behavior. Enable skin stripping only if the intended result is clean netherite rather than destruction.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/faq": "\u003ch2 id=\"requirements\">What does CoreArmorX require?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Paper/Minecraft 1.21.11+ and Java 21+. A permission plugin is optional unless locks are enabled.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"dependencies\">Does it require Vault, PlaceholderAPI, a database or CoreToolsX?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>No. It also needs no GUI library, custom-item plugin or resource pack.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"normal-items\">Do normal upgrades receive plugin data?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>No. Normal upgraded armor remains material-driven vanilla armor.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"dye\">Can leather-skinned armor be dyed?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Yes. Vanilla dye behavior is retained and lore can expose the current color.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"durability\">Can a skin have separate durability?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Yes, but the feature is disabled by default. Configure it globally, by skin or by armor piece.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"unlock-data\">Where is player progression stored?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Nowhere in CoreArmorX. Locks are permission-based.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"reload\">What follows a normal YAML edit?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Run \u003ccode>/corearmorx reload\u003c/code> and review console warnings.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/support-policy": "\u003ch2 id=\"release-channels\">Release channels\u003c/h2>\u003cp>CoreArmorX is free to download and use. Public stable releases are distributed through the official Modrinth project. Paid memberships do not sell the stable plugin.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"supporter-preview-builds\">Supporter preview builds\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Supporters may receive temporary previews, release candidates, staging builds and non-critical hotfix candidates for testing. These builds may be incomplete and are not supporter-exclusive stable releases.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"critical-fix-policy\">Critical fixes\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Confirmed security, exploit, data-loss, major-crash and other critical stability fixes are released publicly when ready. A short preview validation does not create a paid-only fix.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"paid-memberships\">Paid memberships\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Membership may include priority support, setup/configuration review, troubleshooting, debug/log analysis, preview channels, roadmap updates and testing participation. It does not unlock commands, modules, gameplay advantages or server-side functionality.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"discord-authentication\">Discord authentication\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The authentication bot verifies active Patreon membership and assigns Discord roles for supporter channels. The plugin does not require Patreon authentication.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"disclaimer\">Disclaimer\u003c/h2>\u003cp>CoreArmorX is an independent server-side plugin. NOT AN OFFICIAL MINECRAFT PRODUCT. NOT APPROVED BY OR ASSOCIATED WITH MOJANG OR MICROSOFT.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/source-notes": "\u003cp>This documentation targets CoreArmorX 2026.1.2 at plugin revision \u003ccode>4e9aab9851660d84852bf6790f9676c038aa89a9\u003c/code>. Claims were checked against current source, bundled defaults, public feature/configuration documents and the public project identities.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"configuration-source\">Configuration source\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The website synchronizes only \u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>armor-upgrades.yml\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>armor-skins.yml\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>messages.yml\u003c/code> from the private plugin repository. The browser bundle contains public defaults only.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"excluded\">Excluded material\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>plugin.yml\u003c/code>, Java sources, tests, repository metadata, credentials and runtime/player data are excluded. Obsolete BetterCustomArmors-era plans are not documentation sources.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"evidence-limits\">Evidence limits\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Documentation review does not by itself prove a fresh build, live server run, third-party compatibility or production deployment. Paper is the formal runtime contract; marketplace platform tags do not expand it.\u003c/p>\n"
};
  var docs = window.COREX_DOCS;
  if (!docs || !Array.isArray(docs.articles)) throw new Error('Load docs-content.js before docs-bodies.js.');
  // Restore the bodyHtml contract consumed by the wiki, search and full reference.
  docs.articles.forEach(function (article) {
    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(bodies, article.id)) throw new Error('Documentation bundle missing article: ' + article.id);
    article.bodyHtml = bodies[article.id];
  });
}());
